# Agent Guidance: Product Documentation

When creating or organizing product documentation in this directory, refer to [README.md](./README.md) for the documentation hierarchy, artifact types, directory structure, and boundary rules.

## Key rules

- **PRDs, TRDs, user stories, and platform-level scenarios** belong under `docs/product/features/{feature}/`.
- **Surface-specific scenarios** (those whose Given/When/Then language references a specific interaction model) belong under `apps/{surface}/docs/features/{feature}/scenarios/`.
- **Step definitions** (test automation) always belong under each app's test directory, never in `docs/`.
- Before creating the first feature PRD, confirm `docs/product/constitution.md` exists, is approved, and has version metadata.
- Before creating the first feature PRD, confirm `docs/product/vision.md` exists, is approved, and has version metadata.
- If either foundation document is missing, unapproved, or unversioned, complete the Foundation Gate before Requirements.
- Use the Constitution Grill before the Vision Grill when creating foundation documents.
- If product context lives at `docs/product/CONTEXT.md`, ensure root `CONTEXT-MAP.md` points to it so Matt-style `grill-with-docs` agents can discover it.
- Keep `docs/product/CONTEXT.md` limited to glossary and domain language. Put assumptions in vision/research synthesis and decisions in ADRs.
- ADRs default to `docs/adr/` unless the repository already has an ADR convention.
- Every PRD must include a constitution alignment check against every current principle or standard in `./constitution.md`.
- Every TRD must reference its corresponding PRD.
